 Recognizing Phishing and Online Scams
Phishing remains one of the most effective cyberattack methods.
0 Learning to recognize phishing attempts is a critical internet skill.
Common signs include urgent language, requests for personal information,
mismatched sender addresses, and suspicious links. Users should learn to hover over links before clicking, verify the sender's identity through a separate channel,
and never provide sensitive information in response to an unsolicited message.
Regular awareness of evolving scam tactics, such as fake delivery notifications or account suspension alerts, helps users stay one step ahead.
